# Third-party notices

The internal inference backend is derived from [SoulX-FlashHead](https://github.com/Soul-AILab/SoulX-FlashHead), revision `07d3562aec9124a8069ee1cf26eeb440029159f4`, under Apache-2.0. Original source headers are retained. It includes implementations derived from Alibaba Wan and Lightricks LTX-Video; retain their notices when redistributing. Model weights are downloaded separately and retain their original terms.

Local changes: package-relative imports/resources, lazy optional dependencies, configurable compilation, hardware-selected inference precision, PyTorch attention fallbacks for single and multiple GPUs, distributed startup timeouts, and process-isolated serving.

Apple Silicon fork changes by Jim Liddle and contributors (2026): Metal/MPS
device operations, real-valued rotary embeddings for Metal, MPS attention and
synchronization, configurable 384/512 output, and Low-only worker allocation.
Modified vendored files are identified in their source headers. This fork also
adds local Kokoro speech synthesis and browser portrait framing controls.

Local speech uses kokoro-onnx (https://github.com/thewh1teagle/kokoro-onnx)
and Kokoro model/voice assets downloaded during setup. These dependencies and
model assets retain their respective licenses; they are not bundled in this
repository. The sample portrait at samples/meera.jpg is copied from OpenSpline's
docs/videos/livekit/meera.jpg at revision
1e5f2b06e6c3dfc68e59ab9bfb3b30997d51caf9.

